    u('GEN-ECON-09',worked='Ari gives up 24/12 = 2 rugs per lamp; Bea gives up 60/10 = 6 rugs per lamp. Ari has comparative advantage in lamps. For rugs, Bea gives up 1/6 lamp, below Ari\'s 1/2 lamp. A trade of one lamp for four rugs lies between the two lamp costs, so both can gain from specializing and exchanging.')
    u('GEN-ECON-10',check='An estimate from a dense city predicts an 8% ridership gain in a rural area. Which assumption about travel alternatives should the economist examine before applying that estimate?')
