    u('GEN-ECON-16',worked='Demand and supply intersect at a price of $5 and quantity of 150 thousand. Buyers want exactly the amount sellers offer at that point. A price above $5 creates a surplus; a price below $5 creates a shortage. This example finds equilibrium without shifting either curve.',check='At a price below $5 on this graph, which quantity is larger, and what pressure does that create on price?')
    u('GEN-ECON-17',core='A shortage occurs when quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied at the current price. Buyers competing for limited supply put upward pressure on price. A surplus occurs when quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded; sellers then face pressure to lower price. Adjustment tends toward the price where the two quantities are equal.',check='At a price of $4, buyers want 100 thousand gallons and sellers offer 200 thousand. Calculate the imbalance and predict the pressure on price.')
    graph('GEN-ECON-22','tax_incidence')
